findings.body:
**Contain line-listener throws in `createCollector`.**

Line 425 and Line 449 call driver-supplied listeners with no isolation. The `close` handler reaches Line 449 through `stdout.flush()` at Line 526. A listener that throws there skips `settleClose` at Line 528. The `close` promise then never settles, which breaks the `ManagedChild.close` contract ("always settles"). `terminateGracefully` force-resolves, but any caller that awaits `close` directly hangs unless an `uncaughtException` handler exists.

A throw at Line 425 also escapes the `data` handler and skips the remaining lines and the tail update.

`fireRung` already isolates observers this way. Apply the same pattern to the line listeners.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
+  const emit = (line: string): void => {
+    for (const listener of listeners) {
+      try {
+        listener(line);
+      } catch {
+        // a listener throw must not break collection or the close path
+      }
+    }
+  };
...
-        for (const listener of listeners) listener(line);
+        emit(line);
...
-        for (const listener of listeners) listener(finalLine);
+        emit(finalLine);
```
</details>






Also applies to: 449-449
